From: FlipperEmu
Subject: [PATCH] accel/tcg: read a lockless-I/O region without the BQL

memory_region_enable_lockless_io() marks a region whose device does its
own locking, so that an access needs no BQL: prepare_mmio_access() leaves
the lock alone for it. That is the path of a KVM vCPU. TCG's MMIO helpers
take the BQL themselves, for every region, before they dispatch, so under
TCG such a region is locked all the same.

Leave the lock alone for a load of up to 8 bytes from such a region.
Stores and 16-byte loads still take it.

Seen with the Flipper Zero model: the firmware's microsecond delay is a
busy loop on DWT->CYCCNT, a few dozen reads in 9 us. With the BQL taken at
each, a main loop that wanted the lock for a timer got it only once the
vCPU's thread went to sleep for it, and that thread then woke 20 to 50 us
later: a 9 us pulse on a pin lasted 60 us. On 1-Wire that turns a 1 into a
0; about one iButton read in twenty read a ROM of FFs.

Signed-off-by: FlipperEmu
---
--- a/accel/tcg/cputlb.c
+++ b/accel/tcg/cputlb.c
@@ -1977,6 +1977,11 @@
     section = io_prepare(&mr_offset, cpu, full, addr, ra);
     mr = section->mr;
 
+    if (mr->lockless_io) {
+        /* the device does its own locking, as when a KVM vCPU reads it */
+        return int_ld_mmio_beN(cpu, full, ret_be, addr, size, mmu_idx,
+                               type, ra, mr, mr_offset);
+    }
     BQL_LOCK_GUARD();
     return int_ld_mmio_beN(cpu, full, ret_be, addr, size, mmu_idx,
                            type, ra, mr, mr_offset);
